notes = "§The Longroad: \"Every region's main road eventually meets it, which makes it the game's traffic spine\" - the Mirrormarsh's road onto the ring. §Hard and soft gates: the Mirrormarsh's interior needs \"any true light: Hermit's Lantern, Star's Wish, or the Sun unbound\", and without one \"the region loops the player back out\". Modelled here as a refusal to enter - at region granularity the loop and the locked door are the same event. The gate guards ENTRY only: getting lost back out of the fog is what the fog does."

